==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|overshoten}}, {{m|enm|oversheten}}, equivalent to {{pre|en|over|shoot}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{q|noun}} {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈoʊ.vɚˌshut/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-overshoot.wav |Audio (Southern England)}}
* {{q|verb}} {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˌoʊ.vɚˈshut/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-overshoot.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|uːt|s=3}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|countable}} The amount by which something goes too far.
#: {{ux|en|Let's see if we can predict and correct for the '''overshoot'''.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|ecology}} When the population of a species exceeds its environment's [[carrying capacity]].
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Donella Meadows; Jorgen Randers; Dennis Meadows|year=2004|title=Limits to Growth: The 30-Year Update|isbn=978-1-60358-155-4|chapter=Author's preface|passage=With appropriate choice and action such uncontrolled decline could be avoided; '''overshoot''' could instead be resolved by a conscious effort to reduce humanity's demand on the planet.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=James Howard Kunstler|year=2012|chapter=Where We're at|title=Too Much Magic|isbn=978-0802120304|passage=Population '''overshoot''' is therefore unlikely to yield to management. Rather, the usual suspects will enter the scene and do their thing: starvation, disease, {{...}} violence {{...}} [and] death {{...}}.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|title=Systemic Change Driven by Moral Awakening Is Our Only Hope|date=14 August 2017|author={{w|Richard Heinberg}}|work=Ecowatch|url=https://www.ecowatch.com/climate-change-heinberg-2471869927.html|text=Our core ecological problem is not climate change. It is '''overshoot''', of which global warming is a symptom.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable|typography|design}} The portion of a [[letter]] extending above the [[capline]] of other letters of the same [[font]], or the relative degree of such extent.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2019|author=Reece Patton|title=Formatting for Print|passage=The portion resting beyond the capline or baseline is called '''overshoot'''.|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=7siSDwAAQBAJ&pg=PT15}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2020|author=Karen Cheng|title=Designing Type|edition=2nd|page=88|passage=The bowl of the D and the O are usually not identical, as most D forms do not have '''overshoot''' or undershoot.}}

====Translations====
{{trans-top|when the population of a species exceeds its environment's carrying capacity}}
* Hungarian: {{t|hu|túlfogyasztás}}
* Spanish: {{t+|es|sobrecarga|f}}
{{trans-bottom}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|overshoots|overshooting|overshot}}

# To go past something; to go too far.
#: {{ux|en|When you drive, you must remember to not '''overshoot''' the parking space and end up with two wheels over the line.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1961|month=November|title=Talking of Trains: Aircraft on rail tracks|journal=Trains Illustrated|page=650|text=As a result of the accident at Southend Airport when a Hermes aircraft '''overshot''' the runway and fouled the down Shenfield to Southend Victoria line between [[Rochford]] and [[Prittlewell]], the Eastern Region is considering warning arrangements, which have already been provided on some lines running past aerodromes.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2021 December 15|author=Paul Clifton|title=There is nothing you can do|journal=RAIL|issue=946|page=37|text=A ScotRail Driver: [...] A good friend of mine '''overshot''' two stations back-to-back a couple of years ago. He tried to stop at one station and slid by it. Tried to stop at the next station. He slid by that, too.}}
# To [[shoot]] beyond; to shoot too far to hit something.
#* {{RQ:South Twelve Sermons|passage=not to '''overshoot''' his game}}
# To pass swiftly over; to fly beyond.
# {{lb|en|figurative}} To [[exceed]].
#: {{ux|en|to '''overshoot''' the truth}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1782|author=w:William Cowper|title=Poems: by William Cowper, of the Inner Temple, Esq.|oclc=1205032248|chapter=Conversation|text=That fire abated that impells rash youth,<br>Proud of his speed to '''overshoot''' the truth,}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Donella Meadows; Jorgen Randers; Dennis Meadows|year=2004|title=Limits to Growth: The 30-Year Update|isbn=978-1-60358-155-4|chapter=Author's preface|passage=Measured this way humanity was last at sustainable levels in the 1980s. Now it has '''overshot''' by some 20 percent.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2019|author=Reece Patton|title=Formatting for Print|passage=The amount a letter '''overshoots''' is based on the design, but your eye shouldn’t notice it.|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=7siSDwAAQBAJ&pg=PT15}}
# {{lb|en|reflexive}} To venture too far; to [[overreach]] (oneself).

